ready to head into both the grishaverse  and wizarding world  we knew there had to be a reason ben  barnes compared his series shadow and  bone to harry potter  well we did a little research and  spoiler alert  he was right prepare to fall out of your  chair when you hear some of the  similarities we found between the  stories of the sun summoner  and the boy who lived as magic  right away you see that both main  characters alina and harry are orphans  sure harry didn't live in an actual  orphanage like alina did  but they both lost their parents at a  young age ironically  their parents also died for similar  reasons while fighting the darkness  alina's were lost to the fold and  harry's to voldemort and his death  eaters  of course because they were orphans both  never realized the power they held  within  is it just us or do they have the same  premise so far  the one chooses the wizard mr potter  we all know how harry likes to use his  chosen one status  but deep down we know that his prophecy  isn't the life he would have chosen for  himself  being the only one able to defeat  voldemort and save the wizarding world  is probably something he could have  lived without  the same goes for alina who was deemed  as the sun summoner  saint and you guessed it chosen one the  whole first half of season one  is her denying that she is the only one  who can take down the fold  she would trade the little palaces  riches and glories just to be running  around in the army with mao  they both unintentionally become  celebrities and quite frankly the most  important wizard  and grisha in their respective worlds  the stag chose me  there is huge symbolism surrounding the  stag in shadow and bone  the stag is one of the miroseva beasts  that would help amplify  elena's already powerful magic however  throughout the series it also acted as a  beacon of light in her life  and something she had been envisioning  since she was a child  harry certainly didn't get a stag's  bones magically placed underneath the  skin of his collarbone  but it was the shape of his patronus in  both films the stag was a form of  powerful light magic that assisted in  getting rid of the darkness  also known as the fold and dementors  overall the stags in both films just  create such  similar imagery if we didn't know any  better we'd guess they were shots from  the same fictional world  just take a look  [Music]  ah fantasy series and their love for  having manifestations of darkness  it never gets old but in harry potter  and shadow and bone  the darkness looks a little too similar  for us to believe it was purely  coincidental  the fold was created by the darkling  alexander after he channeled dark and  forbidden magic  just like how voldemort used forbidden  magic to create the horcruxes in order  to make himself  immortal but these horcruxes were often  life-threatening to everyone else  just like the vulca creatures created by  the fold let's take a closer look at the  fold and what's inside a horcrux  they're basically identical you should  have stayed and  cut it down at the end of season one  elena thinks they've overtaken the  darkling but she couldn't be more wrong  we get to see that he's actually alive  and stronger than ever and ready to lead  an entire army to battle  sound familiar yup it's just like when  the wizarding world thought one-year-old  harry had defeated voldemort  but he was actually very much alive with  an army of  death eaters ready to support him when  he made his comeback  whether or not alina wins like harry did  has still yet to be seen  we just hope people believe he's back  unlike how minister for magic cornelius  fudge  acted about voldemort that's quite  clever  [Music]  has there ever been a myth or tale in a  fantasy franchise that didn't turn out  to be real  alina being the sun summoner was a myth  and yet here we are  but we want to talk about the myth of  the marozova beasts again these were  animals said to hold  such powerful magic that they'd be able  to elevate egretia's power  like never seen before we couldn't help  but compare that to the story of the  peverell brothers in harry potter  also known as the deathly hallows you  have the invisibility cloak elder wand  and the resurrection stone possessing  all three made a wizard basically  immortal and just like shadow and bone  the most powerful wizard not to mention  they play a key role in defeating  voldemort  and is the way to defeat the fold once  and for all  so does this mean there's still hope  we'll one day receive a hogwarts letter  hogwarts is home and also the safest  place to be in the wizarding world  we know that because it's said many  times throughout the harry potter series  that help will always be given at  hogwarts  to those who ask for it  because of its enchantment spells and  dumbledore being headmaster  it's basically impenetrable well the  grisha and shadow and bone have a  hogwarts of their own  the little palace it's the only place  where grisha can truly be safe and  protected from those who still aren't  fond of the small science they use  or from people who haven't forgotten  them for creating the fold in the first  place  ironically they both happen to be grand  castles  to be fair there is one difference  between the two harry actually wants to  be at hogwarts while  elena can't wait to escape the little  palace  speaking of hogwarts all the wizards who  attend are split into four houses based  on their personalities and ambitions  you have gryffindor slytherin ravenclaw  and hufflepuff  grisha on the other hand are sorted into  orders depending on their powers  corporal alky ethereal key and material  in both series these groups are  differentiated by the color of clothing  they wear  and different crests in harry potter the  main colors are burgundy  green blue and yellow for shadow and  bone the colors are blue  red and purple then the color of their  embroidery tells you what their specific  abilities are  basically the only difference is wizards  wear cloaks and grisha wear keftas  the real question is who do you think is  more powerful  not familiar with the concept what would  a good story be  without the strong bonds of friendship  alina and mal grew up together in the  orphanage and quite literally  don't want to live without one another  sure towards the end of the season  things may have been getting  a little more romantic but it was first  based on a friendship where they would  risk their  lives for one another just like the  golden trio in harry potter  harry hermione and ron would do anything  to protect one another  just think about how hermione and ron  were willing to risk their lives and  become fugitives to help harry find the  horcruxes  none of them would have survived the  series without the other  raise your hand if you think platonic  friendships like this are  totally underrated in tv and movies  you know what i mean no  finally let's talk magic or how  similarly magic works in both  series you might be thinking what do you  mean wizards clearly have more  versatility in their magic over grisha  well that's kind of true but they're  both limited in the same ways  grisha cannot create something that  doesn't already exist they can only  manipulate the matter around them  the same goes for wizards sure they can  accio anything they'd like but they  aren't able to conjure things like money  food and clothing those items must  already exist  and if they did summon them it would be  considered stealing  that's why the weasleys haven't conjured  up a vote full of galleons yet  anyone up for a marathon of these two  stories well the idea for a shadow and  bone film was scrapped in 2012  we can definitely see why they had  originally tied a harry potter producer  to the story  but despite the similarities shadow and  bone and harry potter are still  uniquely their own and let's face it  they are probably some of the best  fantasy content  out there did you find any other  similarities between the two stories
 

